  "id": "Compound::DB06589 - Gene::1565",
  "verbalization": "Pazopanib is shown to bind to Cyp2c8, a cytochrome P450 enzyme, which is involved in the metabolism of various substrates, including arachidonic acid. This binding may inhibit the activity of Cyp2c8, which in turn affects the metabolism of arachidonic acid. The inhibition of arachidonic acid metabolism by Cyp2c8 could lead to the accumulation of arachidonic acid, which is a precursor to pro-inflammatory eicosanoids. This mechanism may contribute to the observed effects of Pazopanib on Cyp2d6, as Cyp2d6 is a downstream participant in the arachidonic acid metabolic pathway. The evidence suggests that Pazopanib exerts its effect on Cyp2d6 through a pathway involving the inhibition of Cyp2c8, which is a key enzyme in the arachidonic acid metabolism. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Cyp2c8 in modulating the activity of Cyp2d6, providing a mechanistic link between Pazopanib and Cyp2d6.",
